# Build context = repository root for every self-built image (images/workbench, images/rustfs-init,
# images/postgres-init, images/gitea-init). The Dockerfiles COPY from images/, notebooks/ and workspace/.
# Patterns without a leading **/ only match at the root, so Markdown files below images/ stay.

# Secrets and local configuration (never bake them into an image layer)
**/.env*

# VCS and editor/tool state
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.dockerignore
.vscode
.idea
.claude

# Not needed by any image
compose*.yaml
compose*.yml
*.md
extensions

# Python / Node / Jupyter artefacts
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/.ipynb_checkpoints
**/node_modules

# Logs and OS noise
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Notebooks: only the shipped examples (notebooks/local/NN-*.ipynb, notebooks/azure/NN-*.ipynb and the configuration
# and helper of the Azure notebooks). Together with workspace/ (README and .gitignore of the repository root) they are
# the seed of the workbench image (/opt/oog/workspace-seed) and of the gitea-init image (first commit of the Gitea
# workspace repository). Other notebooks, outputs and data files must never be baked in.
notebooks/*
!notebooks/local
notebooks/local/*
!notebooks/local/[0-9][0-9]-*.ipynb
!notebooks/azure
notebooks/azure/*
!notebooks/azure/[0-9][0-9]-*.ipynb
!notebooks/azure/azure.config.json
!notebooks/azure/azure_lake.py
